# 🛹 Kickflip OS

### A custom operating system built from the ground up around creativity, customization, and the freedom to make an OS your own.

**Kickflip OS** is a custom operating system project designed and developed by **CodingMonkey55**, also known as **Kim**.

Kickflip OS started with a simple idea:

> **I wanted my own custom operating system.**

Instead of simply using an existing operating system and changing a few settings, themes, icons, wallpapers, and applications, I wanted to create something that felt like **my own project**.

That idea became Kickflip OS.

Kickflip OS is a personal OS project focused on creating a unique desktop experience, custom branding, custom boot screens, custom wallpapers, an installation experience, and a system that can continue growing over time.

The name **Kickflip OS** comes from skateboarding — a kickflip is a classic skateboard trick, and the name represents the style and personality behind the project.

---

## 🛹 About Kickflip OS

Kickflip OS is my custom operating system project.

I created it because I wanted to experiment with operating-system development and build something that wasn't just another default Linux desktop.

The goal is to make an OS that feels recognizable the moment it starts.

From the boot process to the desktop, the installer, wallpapers, system branding, and configuration, Kickflip OS is intended to have its own identity.

This project is also a way for me to learn.

Operating systems are complicated, and Kickflip OS gives me a place to experiment with:

* Bootloaders
* GRUB
* Linux system components
* Live environments
* Installation systems
* Disk installation
* Desktop environments
* System configuration
* Wallpapers
* Themes
* Branding
* Startup screens
* Installer interfaces
* Shell scripts
* Filesystem layouts
* ISO creation
* Bootable USB drives
* Virtual machines
* Hardware compatibility
* And much more

Kickflip OS is a project that can continue evolving as I learn new things.

---

# 👨‍💻 Creator

**Kickflip OS is designed and developed by CodingMonkey55, aka Kim.**

This project is a personal creation and represents my interest in computers, programming, operating systems, customization, and creating something of my own.

I didn't make Kickflip OS because I thought there weren't already enough operating systems.

I made it because **I wanted to make one.**

That's the whole point.

---

# 🎯 Why Kickflip OS Exists

There are thousands of operating systems and Linux distributions available.

But I wanted something different.

I wanted to be able to say:

**"I made this."**

Kickflip OS gives me a project where I can experiment with ideas and build the experience that I want.

The project is not just about making a computer boot.

It's about creating an entire experience.

That includes:

1. Starting the computer
2. Seeing the Kickflip OS boot screen
3. Loading the live environment
4. Opening the installer
5. Setting up an account
6. Connecting to Wi-Fi
7. Selecting an installation drive
8. Confirming the installation
9. Installing the operating system
10. Booting into the finished system
11. Customizing the desktop
12. Using Kickflip OS as a complete operating system

Every part of the experience can become part of the project.

---

# 🛹 The Kickflip Philosophy

Kickflip OS is built around a few simple ideas:

### Make it yours.

The OS should feel customizable rather than generic.

### Have fun building it.

Operating-system development can be complicated, but the project should still be enjoyable.

### Experiment.

Not every feature will work perfectly the first time.

That's part of development.

### Learn by building.

Instead of only reading about how operating systems work, Kickflip OS provides a project where those concepts can actually be tested.

### Keep improving.

Kickflip OS is a project that can grow over time.

